# Browser
# Assist from the caster's side (CR 702.132a), on Bot1's page. Casting Charging Binox, {7}{G}, the page asks whether to choose
# another player to help pay, neither answer pressed by passing; Bot1 asks for help. Bot2, the only other player, makes two
# green mana; then Bot1's page gives it its window for mana abilities - the last before paying, with Cancel, since the spell
# is Bot1's - in which it makes six, and closes it with Done. Bot2 pays {2} of the generic mana; the pool pays the rest.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Forest
Forest
Forest
Charging Binox
Forest x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Charging Binox.Cast
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Charging Binox: choose another player to help pay for it?
? Client.Bot1.Dock = Ask for help; Pay it yourself; Cancel
Bot1.Accept
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Make mana for Charging Binox
? Client.Bot1.Button.Done.Enabled = true
? Client.Bot1.Button.Cancel.Enabled = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.PayCost(X: 2)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Charging Binox.Power = 7
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#1.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#2.Tapped = true
